#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# set_attributes

#% text
# `set_attributes(f, a)` gives the symbol `f` the attribute `a`; `set_attributes(f, [a, b, ...])` several.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `listable`: calls with list arguments map over them; `hold_all`, `hold_first`, `hold_rest`: arguments are passed unevaluated; `orderless` (or `flat`): an associative and commutative head; `effect`: calls perform effects; `handles_failures`: failures arrive as arguments.

#% item
# `protected`, `locked`, `read_protected`, `numeric_function`, `one_identity` and `constant` are accepted and change nothing.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
set_attributes(f1, listable)
f1([1, 2, 3])
#% output
#= [f1(1), f1(2), f1(3)]

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Held arguments:

#% cell
set_attributes(q1, hold_all)
q1(1 + 1)
#% output
#= q1(1 + 1)

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# `clear_attributes` undoes it:

#% cell
set_attributes(f2, listable)
clear_attributes(f2, listable)
f2([1, 2])
#% output
#= f2([1, 2])

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `attributes`, `clear_attributes`, `map`, `quote`
